/*  EXPECTED: COMPILES and runs; compiled output must match the interpreter.

    What a loop over a rabbit's set or chase gives lives in the rabbit, and is copied out. */


Pull a book on collections.
    Define last-word as "outer".
    Define last-letter as "outer".
    Pull a rabbit.
        Define own as a set of text.
        Insert "in" joined to "ner" into own.
        For each word in own, the last-word becomes word.
        Define letters as a chase.
        Insert "abcd" into letters.
        For each letter in letters, the last-letter becomes letter.
    Done.

    /*  Make and drop enough values that freed memory is handed out again. */
    Define churn as a series of text.
    Define tick as 0.
    While tick is less than 400, repeat:
        Insert ("zzzzzzzz" joined to "yyyyyyyy") into churn.
        The tick becomes tick + 1.
    Done.
    State last-word.
    State last-letter.
Done.
